module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.realization_refusal_surfaces_one_phase_late_at_rustc

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data realization_refusal_surfaces_one_phase_late_at_rustc: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "realization_refusal_surfaces_one_phase_late_at_rustc" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "realization refusal surfaces one phase late, at rustc (the compile step reports its verdict -- `0 blocking error(s)` and exit 0 -- while the emitter has written a realization refusal into the emitted crate as compile_error!, so the refusal the emitter decided is first seen by rustc, one phase later, under a build failure nobody joins back to the compile step that reported clean). INVALID STATE: an emitted artifact that carries a refusal while the step that produced it reports admission. HARM: every consumer that trusts the compile verdict -- a lane that emits and hands the crate on, a reader of the compile log -- proceeds on a clean verdict for an artifact that cannot build; the refusal is not lost, but it is relocated to a phase whose failure reads as a toolchain problem.",

    "RECEIPT, 2026-09-19 (lane A of the approval app, milestone A1 of the .dag crypto): `gunbc compile --entry <entry> --target rust` over the closures of std.bitwise, std.bignat, extdeps.crypto.sha2 and extdeps.crypto.nist_p256 printed `0 blocking error(s), 2011 advisory diagnostic(s) (policy: gunbc.compile_clean_diagnostic_policy)` and exited 0 for both entries. `cargo build` of the emitted crates then failed on the runner with 18 compile_error! sites, all `operator realization: host operator `<op>` on structural operand std.integer.<T> -- the declaration has no host realization and declares no operation for this operator`: 16 in the SHA-256 closure (7 `%`, 5 `+`, 2 `-`, 1 `*`, 1 `/`, all on std.integer.UInt32, in std.bitwise and extdeps.crypto.sha2) and those 16 plus 2 `*` on std.integer.UInt8 in std.bignat bignat_from_octets for the P-256 closure. The emitter decided every one of them at emission (std.operator_realization OperatorRealizationRefused, rendered by v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_typed_bin_op through emit_rust_compile_error_expr); none reached the verdict the compile step printed.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the refusal is correct and typed, and the defect is only WHERE it is reported. The emitter's own decision (OperatorRealizationRefused) is a located refusal; what fails is the join from that decision to the step verdict, which counts the policy's blocking diagnostics and does not count refusals the emitter chose to render as compile_error! text. Not the same class as a refusal typed as success: the artifact does not claim to be valid -- it refuses at the next phase -- but the step that owned the decision reported the opposite. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the line does stop, at rustc). CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- every OperatorRealizationRefused the emitter renders is a fact the compile step already holds, so the step verdict can count it as blocking by construction. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the compile step's blocking count includes every realization refusal the emitter rendered into the artifact, SUFFICIENT FOR a closure whose emission carries any compile_error! to be refused by `gunbc compile` itself with the site and message, before any toolchain runs.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.operator_realization", decl_name: "operator_realization_refusal_message", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "emit_typed_bin_op", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.compile_clean_diagnostic_policy", decl_name: "compile_clean_unlisted_import_use_enforcement", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
